  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations are $976M for Nebraska in FY2026 to date. Award count is 14,560 and average award size is $67K. Obligations fell 22.9% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $342M and the Department of Education obligated $289M, making those two agencies the largest buyers so far. NELNET SERVICING LLC received $289M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $154M, making those two vendors the largest recipients. Other notable industry totals include Computer Systems Design Services at $195M and Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $289M. Fiscal-year comparisons show past obligations of $1.3B in FY21, $1.3B in FY22, $2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $1.3B in FY25. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights where federal contract dollars have concentrated by agency, vendor, and NAICS industry through the current fiscal period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What agencies have driven Nebraska federal contract obligations so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $342M and the Department of Education obligated $289M, the two largest buyers. The General Services Administration obligated $165M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $88.6M. Smaller contributors include the Department of Agriculture at $24.6M and the Department of State at $20.4M. Remaining top buyers include the Department of Justice, Department of Homeland Security, Department of the Interior, and Department of Transportation with obligations ranging from $16.8M to $3.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries received the largest shares of Nebraska contract dollars in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "NELNET SERVICING LLC received $289M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $154M, the two largest vendors. Other top vendors include HENDRICKSON TRANSPORTATION LLC at $43.7M and S365 INC at $34.1M. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation totaled $289M and Computer Systems Design Services totaled $195M, followed by Engineering Services at $85.1M."
      }
    ]
